  "Z_tex": "Z = \\tfrac12\\sum N^{D}_{l\\tilde l}\\,N^{A}_{l'\\tilde l'}\\,b^{(l,\\epsilon,l')}\\overline{b^{(\\tilde l,\\epsilon,\\tilde l')}} + \\tfrac12",
  "character_tex": "The $\\mathcal{N}=1$ characters $\\chi^{NS}_{r,s} = q^{-c/24}\\prod_{n\\ge1}\\frac{1+q^{n-1/2}}{1-q^n}\\sum_{k}\\left(q^{a_k}-q^{b_k}\\right)$ and $\\chi^{R}_{r,s} = q^{1/16-c/24}\\prod_{n\\ge1}\\frac{1+q^{n}}{1-q^n}\\sum_{k}\\left(q^{a_k}-q^{b_k}\\right)$, $a_k = \\frac{(2pp'k+p'r-ps)^2-4}{8pp'}$, $b_k = \\frac{(2pp'k+p'r+ps)^2-4}{8pp'}$, $(p,p') = (12,14)$. With $r = l+1$, $s = l'+1$: $b^{(l,0,l')}$ and $b^{(l,2,l')}$ are the parts of $\\chi^{NS}_{r,s}$ at integer and half-integer level (whichever matches the coset weight), and $b^{(l,1,l')} = \\chi^R_{r,s}$.",
  "description": "Coset $SU(2)_{10}\\times SU(2)_2/SU(2)_{12}$ with the (D,A) invariant (D on the level-10 label, A on the level-12 label). Blocks are the coset branching functions $b^{(l,\\epsilon,l')}$ with $(l,\\epsilon,l')\\sim(10-l,2-\\epsilon,12-l')$. The Ramond ground state $(5,1,6)$ is a fixed point of the identification; its two resolved components $b_\\pm$ differ by the constant 1, and the sign keeps $(c/24, c/24)$ as a scalar.",
